# Site Structure & Links (Laravel)

**Web root:** `public/` (Nginx/Apache DocumentRoot).
**Dev data:** `data/` and `docs/` live at project root — not served to the web.

## Page structure (Laravel)

Each public page = **route** + **controller** + **Blade views**:

```
routes/web.php          → URL definition
app/Http/Controllers/   → returns view()
resources/views/pages/{slug}/
  index.blade.php       → @extends('layouts.bdgs'), meta, title, schema
  content.blade.php     → page body only
public/css/bdgs-{slug}.css → page-specific styles
```

Shared shell: `resources/views/layouts/bdgs.blade.php` + `resources/views/partials/bdgs/*`.

## Links & assets — root-relative only

- Internal links and asset `src`/`href` start with `/`: `/services/`, `/css/bdgs-shell.css`.
- **Never** use relative hops (`../`, `./`) or machine paths for internal links.
- **Absolute `https://bdgrowthsuite.com/...` URLs only** in: canonical, `og:url`, Twitter URL, JSON-LD `url`/`@id`, `public/sitemap.xml`, `public/llms.txt`.
- Laravel `route()` / `url()` helpers are fine in PHP; Blade pages use root-relative `/` paths in HTML.

## New page checklist

1. Add route in `routes/web.php` (inside `ProvideMarkdownResponse` middleware group).
2. Create `app/Http/Controllers/{Name}Controller.php`.
3. Create `resources/views/pages/{slug}/index.blade.php` extending `layouts.bdgs`.
4. Create `resources/views/pages/{slug}/content.blade.php` with body markup.
5. Add `public/css/bdgs-{slug}.css` if page needs custom styles.
6. Set `@php($activeNav = '...')` only if page is a top-nav item.
7. Add row to `data/seo-pages.json`; when `status: live`, run `python scripts/build_seo_files.py`.
8. Cross-link 3–5 other live pages from the new content.
9. Run `full-lock-audit` before lock.

## Work-in-progress isolation

- Unfinished pages: build on a git branch; do not set `status: live` in `data/seo-pages.json`.
- Design explorations may live in `docs/variants/**` — not routed until promoted.

## Promote / lock pipeline

1. Build on a branch; extend `layouts.bdgs`.
2. User approves → merge to main.
3. Run `seo-page-audit` / `full-lock-audit` until pass.
4. Set `status: live` in `data/seo-pages.json`; run `python scripts/build_seo_files.py`.
5. Update `docs/progress.md` to `locked`.

## On create / rename / delete

- **Create:** route + controller + views + CSS + `seo-pages.json` row + rebuild SEO files.
- **Rename:** update route, controller, view folder, `seo-pages.json`, inbound links, canonical URLs, rebuild SEO files.
- **Delete:** remove route, controller, views, `seo-pages.json` row, inbound links, rebuild SEO files.

## .md mirrors (AI agents)

No manual `index.md` files. `App\Http\Middleware\ProvideMarkdownResponse` serves markdown at `/{slug}.md` (e.g. `/services.md`, `/index.md` for home). Verify middleware is on the route group.
